You must use different names for different projects. You are using "project" four times.

El jue., 31 ene. 2019 3:37, Zhou Fang <fangzh...@gmail.com> escribió:

> Dear Iñaki Úcar,
>
> Please see my code below. There are four types of projects. Each type of projects use different number of machine A and B with different timeouts. All projects arrive at pre-specified time. Do you think my code correctly reflect the process? Why there is an error message in the end that process project already defined? I didn’t define project anywhere in the code. Thanks!
>

> myData1 <- data.frame(
>   time = c(1:10),
>   priority = 0) %>%
>   dplyr::arrange(time)
>
> myData2 <- data.frame(
>   time = seq(1.1,12,1.2),
>   priority = 1) %>%
>   dplyr::arrange(time)
>
>
> env <- simmer(“project_path")
> env
>

